  m_Name: Phase4_Rheostat
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::STEM.Experiments.Rheostat.RheostatPhase
  instruction: 'Step 4: Dim the lamp with the rheostat.

    Join 3 to 5, 6 to 7,
    and 8 to 4. Run the two voltmeter

    cables from the RS101 to sockets 7 and
    8, then turn the knob.'
  resultText: 'Measurement: V = {V} V, I = {I} A

    Rheostat: R = {R} Ohm



    The
    rheostat is in series with the lamp, so it takes a

    share of the 5 V. More
    resistance leaves less voltage and

    less current for the lamp, so the lamp
    dims.



    Lamp: R = 6.2 V / 0.5 A = 12.4 Ohm

    Check: I = 5 / (12.4 + {R})'
  switchStartsClosed: 1
